Description: Computes and estimates the stress-strength reliability
    R = P(Y < X) (Kotz, Lumelskii and Pensky, 2003, World Scientific)
    for any pair of continuous distributions given by their density and
    distribution functions, including the standard families of 'R' found by
    name. Beyond the single-component model it covers multi-stress
    environments, the three-variable model P(Z < Y < X), s-out-of-k systems
    (Bhattacharyya and Johnson, 1974, <doi:10.2307/2286173>) and cascade
    systems. Parameters are estimated by maximum likelihood, maximum product
    of spacings (Cheng and Amin, 1983,
    <doi:10.1111/j.2517-6161.1983.tb01268.x>), least squares, weighted least
    squares, Cramer-von Mises and Anderson-Darling minimum distance, by
    jackknife and bootstrap bias correction, and by Bayesian
    Metropolis-Hastings sampling. Confidence intervals for R are given by the
    delta method, the parametric bootstrap and posterior intervals, and a
    Monte Carlo engine reports bias, mean squared error and coverage over
    grids of sample sizes and parameter values.
